@eunjae-lee I'm having trouble with this feature using the latest instantsearch.js on Chrome on Mac (latest) - The scroll position isn't restored. However, Safari works fine, even on iOS for me. History within the same page (going back) works as expected though.

* https://infinitehits-cache-m86tvb8nd.now.sh/ - doesn't work in Chrome
* https://infinite-hits-cache-react.now.sh/ - works in all browsers

I tried locally, linking to a local `detail.html` to check if it had anything to do with switching to an external domain (google in the original example). Routing is enabled, so I don't know what's different from the React version.

**UPDATE**

I was able to make the non-React example work by explicitly saving and restoring the scroll position:

```javascript
const search = instantsearch({
  indexName: 'instant_search',
  searchClient,
  routing: true,
});

search.addWidgets([/* setup widgets */]);

window.onbeforeunload = function(e) {
  localStorage.setItem('scrollpos', window.scrollY);
};

search.once('render', () => {
  const scrollpos = localStorage.getItem('scrollpos');
  if (scrollpos) window.scrollTo(0, scrollpos);
});

search.start();
```
